Subject: [PATCH] ikev2: advertise only supported RSA authentication
Track: V26
Status: product
Upstream: not submitted

The pinned authentication dispatcher accepts RSA_SIG (1) but not DIGITAL_SIGNATURE
(14). Its RSA signer/verifier uses SHA1. Advertising RFC 7427 hash algorithms
causes a default stock peer to select an unsupported authentication method.
Remove that advertisement without changing certificate pins, auth dispatch,
cryptographic implementations, or IKE/ESP proposals. Legacy RSA_SIG/SHA1 only.

--- a/src/plugins/ikev2/ikev2.c
+++ b/src/plugins/ikev2/ikev2.c
@@ -5009,13 +5009,7 @@
 			    nat_detection_sha1);
   vec_free (nat_detection_sha1);
 
-  u8 *sig_hash_algo = vec_new (u8, 8);
-  u64 tmpsig = clib_host_to_net_u64 (0x0001000200030004);
-  clib_memcpy_fast (sig_hash_algo, &tmpsig, sizeof (tmpsig));
-  ikev2_payload_add_notify (chain,
-			    IKEV2_NOTIFY_MSG_SIGNATURE_HASH_ALGORITHMS,
-			    sig_hash_algo);
-  vec_free (sig_hash_algo);
+  /* RSA authentication supports legacy RSA_SIG/SHA1 only, not RFC 7427. */
 
   bi0 = ikev2_get_new_ike_header_buff (vm, &b0);
   if (!bi0)
